{"name":"Egret","hex":"#f4ece1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"egret","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various wading birds of the genera Egretta or Ardea that includes herons, many of which are white or buff, and several of which develop fine plumes during the breeding season.","A plume or tuft of feathers worn as a part of a headdress, or anything imitating such an ornament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egret"}],"entries":[{"title":"Egret","blocks":[{"text":"An egret is a type of heron; they are generally long-legged wading birds that have white or buff plumage and develop fine plumes during the breeding season. Egrets are not a biologically distinct group from herons and have the same build."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Ardea_modesta.jpg/330px-Ardea_modesta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egret","wikidata":"Q3060012"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Flying_great_egret_1.jpg/500px-Flying_great_egret_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Flying_great_egret_1.jpg/1280px-Flying_great_egret_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Flying_great_egret_1.jpg/500px-Flying_great_egret_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Great egret in flight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlying_great_egret_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Egrets_in_AP_W_IMG_4220.jpg/500px-Egrets_in_AP_W_IMG_4220.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Egrets_in_AP_W_IMG_4220.